---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import GiveBox from '../components/GiveBox.astro';
import GiftList from '../components/GiftList.astro';
import { facebook, contact } from '../config/site';
import { path } from '../config/paths';
import charcoal from '../assets/photos/charcoal.jpg';
import tux from '../assets/photos/tux.jpg';
---
<Base
  title="Help keep the rescue running"
  description="How your donation keeps Dogs' Best Friend Rescue going: vet care, food, shelter running costs and a carer's wage. Give once or every month."
  current="donate"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Donate</p>
      <h1>Help keep the rescue running</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The dogs at the shelter need looking after every day, not just when there’s an emergency. Regular support is what keeps
        the gates open, the bowls full and the vet bills paid.
      </p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-donate" href="#give">Give now</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-sand">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What your gift pays for</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:20px">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">🩺</span>
          <h3>Vet treatment, medication and emergencies</h3>
          <p>
            Many of the dogs arrive sick or injured. They need check-ups, treatment, medicines, parasite prevention and,
            sometimes, surgery. Emergencies don’t wait for a fundraiser.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">🥣</span>
          <h3>Food for the dogs</h3>
          <p>Every dog at the shelter has to be fed every day. It’s the biggest, most constant need, and it never takes a month off.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">💡</span>
          <h3>Electricity and shelter running costs</h3>
          <p>Electricity, fencing, leads, harnesses and all the other everyday costs. These keep the dogs safe and the shelter working.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">🤝</span>
          <h3>A monthly wage for a carer</h3>
          <p>One staff member helps care for the animals: feeding, cleaning, giving medicines and keeping an eye on every dog. Their wage has to be paid every month.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>Why monthly gifts matter most</h2>
        <p>
          One-off donations often come in when people see an emergency. They’re a huge help. But the shelter’s bills arrive every month,
          whatever happens.
        </p>
        <p>
          A regular gift, even a small one, lets the rescue know what’s coming in. That means planning food orders, booking vet care
          and paying the carer without worrying about next month.
        </p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Predictable money for predictable costs</li>
          <li>Less time spent asking for emergency help</li>
          <li>More time spent with the dogs</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <Image src={tux} alt="Tux, a black rescue dog with floppy ears, resting his chin on a wooden bench" widths={[480, 900]} sizes="(min-width: 820px) 45vw, 100vw" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-sand">
    <div class="narrow">
      <GiveBox heading="Give to the dogs" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Or pick something specific</p>
      <h2>What a gift can buy</h2>
      <GiftList />
      <blockquote style="margin-top:24px">
        All donations go towards food, shelter, medication and health care for all our dogs. Any remaining funds go to our outreach
        programmes and services: education in local schools, sterilisation clinics and Freedom Flight costs. If you’d like to pay for
        a specific item, please <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>contact us</a>.
      </blockquote>
      <p style="margin-top:16px">
        Prefer to support one dog, or join the Association? <a href={path('/get-involved/#sponsor')}>Sponsor a dog</a> or
        <a href={path('/membership/')}>become a member</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap split">
      <Image src={charcoal} alt="Charcoal, a black dog with large upright ears, sitting on a tiled floor wearing a collar" widths={[330]} sizes="330px" style="max-width:330px;margin-inline:auto" />
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What vet care can mean</p>
        <h2>Charcoal’s legs</h2>
        <p>
          Charcoal was dumped at a temple as a puppy with her brother Noodles and grew up in foster care. She has luxating patellas,
          which is why her back legs are wonky. It never slowed her down.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2022 the rescue estimated her surgery and physical therapy at 40,000 to 50,000 baht. That’s the kind of cost a small rescue
          faces on top of the everyday bills, and why steady support matters.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-brown">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Can’t give money right now?</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div><h3>Share</h3><p>Share the rescue’s <a href={facebook.url} rel="noopener">Facebook posts</a> with friends who love dogs.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Fly with a dog</h3><p>Flying to the USA, Canada or Europe? <a href={path('/contact/')}>Tell us</a> your date, airline and destination. An adopted dog may be able to travel with you.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Ask about something specific</h3><p>Want to pay for a particular item or a particular dog’s care? <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>Email us</a>.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
